abstract: >-
  A packing of 12 unit cubes in a cube of side 2.9315185094797, below the previous best known
  2.9327717687048653 (H. Lin, July 2026), found by hardening balls into cubes under inward pressure
  and certified in exact rational arithmetic. Includes the claim file, a 30-line verifier, an exact
  certificate, simulators for squares and cubes, the paper and the full experiment log.
keywords:
  - packing
  - cubes in a cube
  - squares in a square
  - computational geometry
  - discrete geometry
